# assets/packs/ — every third-party pack, licensed or reference, QUARANTINED
# under one root so one rule covers them all. Licensed packs are NEVER
# committed: the licenses permit use in a project but not redistribution as
# an asset, and this repo is public. Reference packs (Character Creator 2D)
# ride the same rule — pose grammar, not architecture, and not ours.
assets/packs/
# Safety net, unanchored on purpose: a pack unpacked anywhere OUTSIDE the
# quarantine is still caught by name shape before the next `git add -A` —
# which is exactly how NEW-TopDownCharacter-v1.3 reached master in 4c384a9.
*TopDownCharacter*/
*Pixel Art*/
# regenerable sprite outputs — the whole roster (scripts/roster_mold.py)
# plus the System A walk-off strips (scripts/cipher32_walk.py); the
# committed scripts are the decision records, the pixels rebuild.
# assets/original/ is deliberately ABSENT here: PixelLab rolls are
# stochastic and the .aseprite hand-work is unique — nothing there
# rebuilds, so it is tracked source art (original_body_pipeline.md, D9).
assets/sprites/

# walkable harness deps (prototypes/walkable/test)
node_modules/

# Audition captures — screenshots a human judges, regenerated by
# prototypes/walkable/test/audition_generated.mjs on demand.
prototypes/walkable/test/audition-*/
